  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Let $V={R}_{1}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $1$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $f(t)=5t$ and $g(t)=7t-8$ with respect to the inner product.",
  "worked_solution": "The distance between $f(t)=5t$ and $g(t)=7t-8$ with respect to the given inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\u2016f(t)-g(t)\u2016 \\\\  & =\u20165t-(7t-8)\u2016 \\\\  & =\u2016-2t+8\u2016 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\u27e8-2t+8,-2t+8\u27e9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8-2t+8,-2t+8\u27e9 & =(-2t+8){|}_{0}\\cdot (-2t+8){|}_{0}+(-2t+8){|}_{1}\\cdot (-2t+8){|}_{1} \\\\  & =8\\cdot 8+6\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{100}=10.$",
